{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:18305173 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:18305173 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"18305173","source":"MED","pmid":"18305173","pmcid":"PMC2265198","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC2265198"]},"doi":"10.1073/pnas.0708874105","title":"MHC class II stabilization at the surface of human dendritic cells is the result of maturation-dependent MARCH I down-regulation.","authorString":"De Gassart A, Camosseto V, Thibodeau J, Ceppi M, Catalan N, Pierre P, Gatti E.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"De Gassart A","lastName":"De Gassart","firstName":"Aude","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0574-344X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre d'Immunologie de Marseille-Luminy, Université de la Méditerranée, Case 906, 13288 Marseille Cedex 9, France."}]}},{"fullName":"Camosseto V","lastName":"Camosseto","firstName":"Voahirana","initials":"V"},{"fullName":"Thibodeau J","lastName":"Thibodeau","firstName":"Jacques","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Ceppi M","lastName":"Ceppi","firstName":"Maurizio","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Catalan N","lastName":"Catalan","firstName":"Nadia","initials":"N"},{"fullName":"Pierre P","lastName":"Pierre","firstName":"Philippe","initials":"P","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0863-8255"}},{"fullName":"Gatti E","lastName":"Gatti","firstName":"Evelina","initials":"E","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0667-0799"}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0574-344X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0667-0799"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0863-8255"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","recommended_reviews","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"9","volume":"105","journalIssueId":1512645,"dateOfPublication":"2008 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":2008,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","essn":"1091-6490","issn":"0027-8424","isoabbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","nlmid":"7505876"},"printPublicationDate":"2008-03-01"},"pubYear":"2008","pageInfo":"3491-3496","abstractText":"In response to Toll-like receptor ligands, dendritic cells (DCs) dramatically enhance their antigen presentation capacity by stabilizing at the cell-surface MHC II molecules. We demonstrate here that, in human monocyte-derived DCs, the RING-CH ubiquitin E3 ligase, membrane-associated RING-CH I (MARCH I), promotes the ubiquitination of the HLA-DR beta-chain. Thus, in nonactivated DCs, MARCH I induces the surface internalization of mature HLA-DR complexes, therefore reducing their stability and levels. We further demonstrate that the maturation-dependent down-regulation of MARCH I is a key event in MHC class II up-regulation at the surface of LPS-activated DCs. MARCH I is, therefore, a major regulator of HLA-DR traffic, and its loss contributes to the acquisition of the potent immunostimulatory properties of mature human DCs.","affiliation":"Centre d'Immunologie de Marseille-Luminy, Université de la Méditerranée, Case 906, 13288 Marseille Cedex 9, France.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Dendritic Cells","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cells, Cultured"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ubiquitin-Protein Ligases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descr